Population Density by LGA
The Gambia’s urbanization from 2013 to 2024 led to a decrease in Banjul's population density but
a sharp rise in Kanifing and Brikama, driven by economic growth. Rural areas saw modest
increases as migration to urban centers continued. National population density grew from 174 in
2013 to 227 people per square kilometer in 2024.
